  "query_preview": "../ Monday to Saturday / Monday will see a frontal band\ntrying to push across the gulf with a weaker ridge feature across\nthe panhandle area. Drier weather will be continuing to start left\nover from Sunday. As the parent low of the frontal feature is\nholding over the central Bering Sea the front in weakening as it\ngets closer winds will be diminishing, think that they will stay\nbelow Gale with the Tuesday front and not seeing significant\nprecipitation amounts. Through the midweek and towards weekend the\ngeneral pattern continues to look on active side with any\npotential shortwaves about the Bering Sea low being pushed into\nthe Gulf of Alaska  \n\nThe closer to the weekend Long range solutions starting to suggest\na stronger surface low moving towards the west Central Aleutians,\nwhich would push ridge to the western gulf that will shift the\nflow pattern around and my bring another break in the\nprecipitation for the SE AK panhandle.",
